# Units declared by scripts/40-vendor-parity-snapshot.sh (verify + baseline modes).
#
# `text` and `hash` are DATA producers -- their stdout is piped into `shasum` and
# into diffs -- so they deliberately emit no receipt. Only the two gate modes do.
#
# The `snapshot` unit exists because an empty snapshot compared against an empty
# baseline diffs clean and reports parity over nothing at all.

snapshot
baseline-compare
